The following parts are third-party or derived works.

ReadableRH/Window/, ReadableRH/Host/
  Taken from L. Alpöge's Lean project (alpo.ge, November 2026). Only the
  import lines and module names are changed; the proofs are his work.

ReadableRH/FunctionalEquation.lean, ReadableRH/LogDeriv.lean
  The functional-equation step and the order-of-vanishing lemma follow the
  same project.

corollaries/Vinogradov.lean, corollaries/Vinogradov/  (Apache License 2.0,
  corollaries/LICENSE-APACHE)
  From https://github.com/anaxia-research/Breakthrough-problems-3 (directory lean/),
  by Deep Bhattacharjee. Changed here: the files that used the half-plane
  `zeroFree` directly take it as an instance argument
  `[Fact Main.ZeroFree]`, and Vinogradov/Final.lean and
  Vinogradov/EulerKronecker/Final.lean are removed; the instance is supplied
  by corollaries/LiouvilleEnergyRH/Unconditional.lean. The headers of
  Vinogradov/MRT.lean, Vinogradov/Riesz.lean, Vinogradov/ContourShift.lean and
  Vinogradov/EulerLog.lean name the OpenAI files they adapt.

corollaries/OAI/  (Apache License 2.0, corollaries/LICENSE-APACHE)
  OpenAI, the Lean library of https://github.com/openai/math, copied
  unchanged, restricted to two import closures:
  - the import closure of OAI.NumberTheory.DirichletL.Nonvanishing
    (2,924 files, as vendored in anaxia-research/Breakthrough-problems-3, directory
    lean/OAI; byte-identical to openai/math), which proves the zero-free
    half-plane `OAI.DirichletCharacter.LFunction_ne_zero_of_seven_eighths_lt_re`
    used by corollaries/LiouvilleEnergyRH/Unconditional.lean. It contains
    OAI/NumberTheory/DirichletL/LogarithmicControl.lean, used by
    Vinogradov/ and LiouvilleEnergyRH/;
  - the import closure of OAI.NumberTheory.TwoPointCorrelations.FinalMain
    (1,539 files), which proves the two-point theorem
    `OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.liouville_log_saving` used by
    corollaries/LiouvilleEnergyRH/TwoPointChowla.lean.

